// EXPECTED: compile error
// expect-error: @truncate has no meaning on a float
//
// BUG-802 — @truncate means "keep the low bits"; a float has none. It used to
// emit a bare C cast, i.e. the same undefined out-of-range conversion the plain
// cast had. The diagnostic names both defined replacements: @saturate (clamp)
// and (T)v (range-checked).
u32 main() {
    f64 v = 3.5;
    u32 x = @truncate(u32, v);
    return x - 3;
}
